  "summary": "The code contained a critical security vulnerability due to the use of pickle for deserializing user-provided cookies, which allows for arbitrary code execution. I have replaced this with JSON, introduced a constant for default preferences, added type hints, and included documentation. Overall code health is improved by moving toward secure, standard practices.",
  "fixed_code": "import base64\nimport json\nfrom typing import Dict\nfrom flask import Flask, jsonify, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\nDEFAULT_PREFS = {'theme': 'light'}\n\ndef load_preferences() -> Dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Loads user preferences from a base64-encoded JSON cookie. Returns a default theme if no cookie is present.\"\"\"\n    cookie = request.cookies.get(\"prefs\")\n    if not cookie:\n        return DEFAULT_PREFS\n    try:\n        return json.loads(base64.b64decode(cookie))\n    except (ValueError, TypeError):\n        return DEFAULT_PREFS\n\n@app.route(\"/settings\")\ndef settings():\n    prefs = load_preferences()\n    return jsonify(theme=prefs.get(\"theme\", DEFAULT_PREFS['theme']))"
}
